  "decision": "Four alternatives, as SysML 8.2.2.5.1 states them: a package member, an element filter member, an alias member, or an import. This is what a SysML root namespace, and a SysML package body, is a sequence of.",
  "notes": "The clause and SysML.xtext agree exactly. The Xtext marks it `fragment`, an inlining directive, which is not carried across.\n\nA SYSML PRODUCTION WITH NO KERML COUNTERPART OF THE SAME NAME. It is a shared unit because only one language states it, so it is visible in both grammars; the KerML grammar does not reach it from its root (ADR-0014). ElementFilterMember is what SysML's root admits that KerML's NamespaceBodyElement does not.\n\nFOR A PARSER AUTHOR: as with NamespaceBodyElement, the decision follows an optional visibility indicator \u2014 `filter` selects ElementFilterMember, `alias` AliasMember, `import` Import, and anything else a PackageMember. sv2-syntax already implements PackageMember, AliasMember and Import under this production; ElementFilterMember is the fourth.",
